{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/218017-unveiled","id":218017,"title":"Unveiled","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-08-04T04:28:25-07:00","id":218017,"title":"Unveiled","content":"Presume some Scions do something so obvious and so over the top that it is impossible (given the information age) to keep it under wraps. What then would the reaction of the world be? We're talking about giving the whole world conclusive, empirical evidence that not only do the old gods exist, but they have power, and power that is more immediate and effective than anything we've seen in thousands of years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-04T07:40:32-07:00","id":218137,"title":"","content":"The everyday person's reaction depends on how the revelation came about. Most people who are too old to read Percy Jackson won't believe you're a child of Zeus no matter what you do. They'll either believe that you're powerful but have a different explanation for your powers or that you're a fake. If the revelation was on TV, most will believe it's faked.<br /> <br /> As for large groups, it also depends on how the revelation occurred but will probably be more predictable:<br /> <br /> Governments: move to defend themselves from the new powers by seeking out powers of their own. Since this is an action game, some might initiate pre-emptive strikes.<br /> <br /> Churches: publicly denounce the new false gods. Since this is an action game, some might decide to burn these witches themselves.<br /> <br /> Corporations: how does the revelation affect their bottom line, and can they benefit from it? Since this is an action game, some might decide that further research is necessary and that the so-called gods' rights are less important than scientific and financial progress.<br /> <br /> Scientists: immediate attempts to understand and catalog these new beings. Well, right after they manage to prove experimentally that it isn't a hoax. Since this is an action game, some might find ways to enhance powers while others find ways to dampen them. Still others may seek to capture scions for experimentation and even look for ways to bend the godlings' ichor to their own ends.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Need some online tools, including a Scion/Exalted battle wheel? <a href=\"http://rpg-tools.org/generators/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">http://rpg-tools.org/generators/index.php</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/829-james-mcmurray","name":"James McMurray","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-04T09:35:56-07:00","id":218266,"title":"","content":"That's assuming anyone wasted their time reading Percy Jackson.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-04T09:39:38-07:00","id":218271,"title":"","content":"A one-off thing can be written off as a fake, but the more often it happens, the more publicly it happens, the more likely it is people are going to accept there's _some_ reality to it - after all, extraordinary evidence is being demonstrated on a repeatable basis.<br /> <br /> Then there's everything that comes with the Scions - followers, creatures, titanspawn...<br /> <br /> And in a 2e campaign, you're also going to have sorcerers, oracles and holy people demonstrating people can develop certain powers, that they're drawing from the myths, and that there's something powerful associated with the myths.<br /> <br /> It'll get to the point people acknowledge something above and beyond current scientific understanding is going on here, that people are suddenly gaining superhuman powers, that mythic creatures and monsters, and modernised versions of same, are crawling out of the woodwork... The effect on the sciences alone would be cataclysmic, as what we know gets turned upside down.<br /> <br /> You may get a number of general viewpoints:<br /> <br /> * All of this is inspired by mythology.<br /> * All of this is the inspiration for mythology.<br /> * All of this _is_ mythology updated for the present day.<br /> <br /> You're going to get the mercenary, seeking to make use of these powers; the researchers, seeking to understand what's going on here; the spiritual seekers, looking for faith or meaning; the suspicious, wondering if this is all it seems; the believers, who accept this is what it appears to be; the believers with a grudge, who want to know where the gods have _been_ all this time; the media, looking for something that's going to get more eyeballs - 'cause you'd better believe this'd get eyeballs by the plenty, since it's good spectacle; and yet more besides.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-04T09:41:40-07:00","id":218274,"title":"","content":"Or just get someone to use Rumor Mill to get a &quot;wow, neato keen, the old gods are real and their kids live among us&quot; campaign going.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-04T20:35:47-07:00","id":218728,"title":"","content":"Lets up the ante and make it even more obvious;<br /> <br /> More than a hundred ppl capture live-action footage of some Miscellaneous Scion of Thor kicking a 2-story firedrake's ass with &quot;Mjunior&quot; his enchanted claw-hammer, a glorious battle to be sure...but one that leaves a 2 story tall corpse laying in the middle of a major thoroughfare which must then be cleaned up by city sanitation. No way in hell it could be a hoax. Think it might take more than that to induce worldwide hysterical panic?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-04T21:12:10-07:00","id":218761,"title":"","content":"It all really depends on how active the Gods, magical creatures and other Scions of the setting are. With Epic Socials, it's child's play to sway mortals. Spin it however you want and the world dances to your tune. Call up a few key people, Social them into your brainslaves and then go on TV, use some Knacks and boom. Positive press from every direction.<br /> <br /> My players are currently teetering on the edge of revealing the supernatural to the world. They're opposed by Agents, tall, skinny, sunglass-wearing suited people that seem unusually resilient when faced with supernatural power, are armed with Legend-draining weapons and can detect &quot;Aberrant Entities&quot; via their special sunglasses. The Agents claim to work for the US government. It isn't just the spooks that are opposing them, though. One of the PC's is against it, because of the chaos it might unleash. Several NPCs have expressed doubts about it.<br /> <br /> What will happen if the supernatural <i>is</i> revealed? It's hard to tell and it depends entirely on the actions of the PCs. <br /> <br /> At least, that's how I think most Scion games should work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-04T23:52:59-07:00","id":218893,"title":"","content":"Also depends on where they make the reveal.<br /> <br /> If they do it somewhere like the US the response will be very diferent to the response if they were in Papua New Guinea or Yemen or something.<br /> <br /> Personally I'm planning on running a game where the PCs will eventually reveal all and Scions become the new celebrities, column inches spilled debating whether Nguyen, Scion of Aphrodite prefers short or long hair and what the Scion of Set uses as their weight loss diet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-05T03:01:38-07:00","id":218942,"title":"","content":"All great food for thought!<br /> <br /> It is an interesting parallel, but it looks like revealing the mythological world would logically have much the same consequences that the eruption of Novas did in Aberrant. It makes sense considering how all these previous examples of mythical heroes (Perseus, Beowulf, Gilgamesh, etc...) were probably recognize-on-sight celebrities on their heyday, and with our current media soaked culture you'd end up with the same thing happening. Of course, we're so jaded now that it's likely to quickly fade from popularity without epic socials backing it up constantly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T08:38:13-07:00","id":223298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/218017-unveiled?p=218893#post218893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also depends on where they make the reveal.<br /> <br /> If they do it somewhere like the US the response will be very diferent to the response if they were in Papua New Guinea or Yemen or something.<br /> <br /> Personally I'm planning on running a game where the PCs will eventually reveal all and Scions become the new celebrities, column inches spilled debating whether Nguyen, Scion of Aphrodite prefers short or long hair and what the Scion of Set uses as their weight loss diet.</div> </div> </div> </div>In Telgar's game, we attempted to do it on Oprah. Before the damn agents shut down the feed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T18:34:02-07:00","id":223746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/218017-unveiled?p=218893#post218893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also depends on where they make the reveal.<br /> <br /> If they do it somewhere like the US the response will be very diferent to the response if they were in Papua New Guinea or Yemen or something.<br /> <br /> Personally I'm planning on running a game where the PCs will eventually reveal all and Scions become the new celebrities, column inches spilled debating whether Nguyen, Scion of Aphrodite prefers short or long hair and what the Scion of Set uses as their weight loss diet.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ah. The Aberrant approach. Which pretty much makes sense when you consider, as Telgar said, a few social knacks in the right place and you can get awesome press any time you want it. It's a big reason that Resources/Wealth/Money was never a background. It's too easy to get to be worthwhile spending points on. Same with publicity. Maybe instead of N! from Aberrant there will be a S! channel documenting what those crazy Scions are doing next. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2608-squee","name":"Squee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2608_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T22:45:54-07:00","id":223885,"title":"","content":"How the world responds to the revelation that A) The &quot;pagan&quot; religions are actually pretty freakin' relevant beyond revivalists and academia, B) That these gods are having children who are pretty much badasses destined to become mythic themselves and C) Not only are there Gods but really nasty Monsters that wanna eat you -- all of this depends on the type of Chroonicle theme you're trying to run.<br /> <br /> You could definitely go the Telgar's Game route and have Scions go into the celebrity limelight with (I think) MIBs trying to shut things down because mortal celebrities already have enough power/influence.<br /> <br /> You could run how others have done it and Scions actually have to remain behind a veil of secrecy because there's a really good reason to keep it all hush-hush.<br /> <br /> I've done several reactions and each was tailored to the sort of game I wanted to run. Generally though, what's already been said will work for a 1st time game or even just a setting where the focus on more on Divine antics and less on mortal interactions.<br /> <br /> In my New York Post-Apocalyptic game, Scions are forming into bands and creating enclaves that are tailored to each group's personality and needs. Mortal law is effectively brought under Hero-level control and it'll deal with more how each Enclave treats and uses the humans who entrust their safety to the Heroes. Alas, they tried Oprah and got her eaten. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T01:58:53-07:00","id":223976,"title":"","content":"This all makes me curious to see any revamped fatebinding rules since the power of modern media makes shaping one's own role a lot easier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T18:34:36-07:00","id":225516,"title":"","content":"For starters, a giant &quot;told you so&quot; from Hindus and other polytheists.<br /> <br /> It also depends on immediate spin control, and how well certain knacks work on large crowds of people via mass-media platforms. I could see an immediate military reaction of &quot;quash&quot; which, IMHO, would be relatively effective on low-power scions.<br /> <br /> The Abrahamic religions start immediately using the revelation and looking for ways to spin it to prove the existence of Yahweh (whether or not that deity actually exists in whatever setting you're running), though many likely change faiths instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Games are a way for us to explore what it means to be human, or inhuman, as the case may be. Let's all have a good time playing them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/400-guitarsniper","name":"guitarsniper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T17:02:19-07:00","id":226596,"title":"","content":"The immediate &quot;quash&quot; reaction that would come from the paranoid 1st and 2nd world military does make sense. But maybe low level scions wouldn't be as defenseless as one might think. Even an army of soldiers is still just a mass of mortals, all of whom can be quelled with Crowd Control.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T20:43:29-07:00","id":226756,"title":"","content":"crowd control ain't going to help you against a Tomahawk missile that doesn't have a mind for you to affect. The real danger zone would be when Scions' presence was known but their capabilities were still uncertain, because in that case the response would, in my opinion, trend towards overkill.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Games are a way for us to explore what it means to be human, or inhuman, as the case may be. Let's all have a good time playing them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/400-guitarsniper","name":"guitarsniper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T05:58:27-07:00","id":230114,"title":"","content":"And then you write chart for military weapon like missile, grenade and nuclear weapon <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> In the event that you unveil god and titan I think you make earth a valid ground for world wide war. Titans know how powerful are the prayer from humanity to gods and would probably want to divert them or destroy them. It's common thinking to destroy/capture the resources of your ennemy in war time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2799-astoril","name":"Astoril","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2799_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T09:58:08-07:00","id":230309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>guitarsniper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/218017-unveiled?p=226756#post226756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">crowd control ain't going to help you against a Tomahawk missile that doesn't have a mind for you to affect. .</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why the character with the mad social skills teamed up with the former baseball player with high strength and dexterity, Relic bat and a very visually fun stunt....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T12:51:49-07:00","id":230453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astoril</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/218017-unveiled?p=230114#post230114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Titans know how powerful are the prayer from humanity to gods and would probably want to divert them or destroy them. It's common thinking to destroy/capture the resources of your ennemy in war time.</div> </div> </div> </div>In Scion, prayers have no benefit at all. Gods don't need humans to worship them and they don't get any benefit from it. The single exception are the Aztecs, who do get some benefit from blood sacrifices.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T14:02:56-07:00","id":230527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/218017-unveiled?p=230453#post230453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In Scion, prayers have no benefit at all. Gods don't need humans to worship them and they don't get any benefit from it. The single exception are the Aztecs, who do get some benefit from blood sacrifices.</div> </div> </div> </div>Man, I had to go with Quetzalcoatl as my god parent.....<br /> <br /> Well, a cactus thorn stabbed into my tongue, earlobes, lips or genitals isn't the worst thing I can think of. Close, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T14:33:36-07:00","id":230563,"title":"","content":"AFAIK, it's not super explicit in the books, and it's also totally a ST call. I happen to believe that prayer is sort of like an overdrive. Gods are powerful without it, but those who do receive prayer are more so, though not necessarily in a mechanical sense. But that's just my opinion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Games are a way for us to explore what it means to be human, or inhuman, as the case may be. Let's all have a good time playing them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/400-guitarsniper","name":"guitarsniper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T04:41:19-07:00","id":231315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/218017-unveiled?p=230453#post230453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In Scion, prayers have no benefit at all. Gods don't need humans to worship them and they don't get any benefit from it. The single exception are the Aztecs, who do get some benefit from blood sacrifices.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I have to disagree. Worshippers are the reasons of why the ancient Gods still exist. That's how Gods and Mortals survive. Because both co-exist. That's what Fate is about.<br /> <br /> &quot;Their forms rely on mortal beliefs to keep them coherent and free from merger with their Titan parents. What is this amazing power that mortals have, of which they are entirely unaware? In short, it\u2019s Story.&quot; Hero p.220<br /> <br /> <br /> If the world is to know something about supernatural, I think Scions should have already been exposed, if science is more advanced than what they show us on TV (e.g. X-men). Any Youtube video might have attracted any scientists attentions. And my guess is mortals would see that something like &quot;wow&quot; and nothing else. But scientists and the government would want to know more. And until the government makes the information public (and even that might not be enough), the mortals won't believe their eyes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T07:42:10-07:00","id":231492,"title":"","content":"The books waffle on this a very very very little bit. You've cited one of the few statements that go the &quot;people matter&quot; way to the dozens that say &quot;humans can go fuck all&quot;.<br /> <br /> And mutually contradictory fluff aside, the reality of the game, crunch-wise, is that humans matter insofar as they can affect dice pools because of Fatebound roles (except for their delicious blood and pain if you are Aztec or a Magic using butcher-type). That's about it. Otherwise they are about as important as tissue paper. Occasionally useful, but very disposable. They can pray until they are blue in the face, but it's not going to hurt or help the prayee in the slightest unless he happens to be in the room and trying to do something very un-him-like or very him-like. <br /> <br /> So, Loki can wear a cheap plastic Marilyn Monroe mask (make it look good) and convince the people of Earth to do pretty much everything he wants....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T10:05:06-07:00","id":231621,"title":"","content":"Loki...Lets change that to &quot;Coyote&quot; and the cart gets all turned over.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T10:39:03-07:00","id":231645,"title":"","content":"Try disposing every single mortal... and Gods would be useless... they exist because of mortals. They exist for the mortals. No God would be foolish enough to let things go wrong. They have to save their asses AND mortals'. The Gods are powerful but aren't crazy. They won't create a tsunami unless they are forced to. Even the moodiest ones won't.<br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure Loki and Coyote have better tricks to do than embodying Monroe for Gods know what... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T13:36:24-07:00","id":231917,"title":"","content":"Why would they be useless? They don't exist because of mortals. They were here before mortals. They created mortals. Hell, they've created mortals, destroyed mortals and created them again in several iterations. I guess they created them for some reason or other. They must be useful for something. But they don't NEED them. It doesn't even make sense without a lot tricksy maneuvering, through some chicken and broken eggs territory: How can the existence of the gods be predicated on the existence of mortals, if mortals were created by the gods? The gods could not have existed without the mortals' belief. The mortals could not have existed without the gods' existing to create them. QED Nothing exits. <br /> <br /> Witness the Greek gods. Sure all those sacrifices smell good, but the gods don't NEED them, they make them predisposed to grant favors or withhold punishments. The gods NEED nectar and ambrosia. <br /> <br /> This whole &quot;belief creates the gods&quot; and &quot;belief empowers the gods&quot; meme isn't really germane to the Scion setting. It's a complete anachronism and has a lot of traction in the gaming community through it's perpetuation in some of the original RPGs. But it's not definitive and isn't even relevant in a game about the fundamentals of mythology. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T17:44:09-07:00","id":232151,"title":"","content":"I could take some of that same argument and inject Native Americana and just watch as the thread explodes in hypocrisy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T18:34:15-07:00","id":232179,"title":"","content":"Please explain? Because I don't see how the Native Americans have anything to do with Gods existing without a need for mortals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T18:52:21-07:00","id":232184,"title":"","content":"In Scion 1e, maybe mortals have no power over Gods. But that's contradictory with what's written in the Fate part. The Fate part is the most funny, amazing and the trickest part of the game. No powers can't be used without involving mortals. That's how powerful a mortal is. Because risking mortals' lives aren't what Gods do for fun. Some does, but not all of them. In fact, it seldom happened. <br /> I'm not saying that a God cannot kill a mortal easily. Of course they can. But there are expectations and Gods cannot always act against that. You are not born or become the God of Harvest and leave the fields empty. Hades will always have to guard the Deaths not because he's willing to, but because he's assigned to. Scions will be even more inclined to do what they will do once Gods. Helping or destroying the mortals would be part of their God roles. So, yeah. mortals are that much important to the game. Because they help Scions to become the Gods they will be. That's how I see it.<br /> <br /> The game is only fun to play when mortals' lives are at stake. Making Gods and Scions protecting them, I'd say it's one hell of a power! They don't even need to do the dirty work. They scream, get scared, cry... sometimes die and part of the world is safe for a while!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T19:43:44-07:00","id":232273,"title":"","content":"Eh. That's how you wanna run it mate, sure. But the most Fatebonds can do under the as-written system is apply a few piddly dice of penalties. Gods don't care about 1-5 dice of penalties because they're throwing around 40+ automatic successes. Powers don't need mortals to work, that's silly.<br /> <br /> If Thor throws a lightning bolt at Jormungandr, there doesn't need to be a mortal witness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T19:51:17-07:00","id":232284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/218017-unveiled?p=232273#post232273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh. That's how you wanna run it mate, sure. But the most Fatebonds can do under the as-written system is apply a few piddly dice of penalties. Gods don't care about 1-5 dice of penalties because they're throwing around 40+ automatic successes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those dice penalties should be quite a bit higher, in the 40-100 dice penalty range. Of course there is a minimum amount of dice you can have, so it is not really painful unless you are using a lot of dice adders like Animal Aspect.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1505-charles-red","name":"Charles Red","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T22:54:26-07:00","id":232471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/218017-unveiled?p=232273#post232273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh. That's how you wanna run it mate, sure. But the most Fatebonds can do under the as-written system is apply a few piddly dice of penalties. Gods don't care about 1-5 dice of penalties because they're throwing around 40+ automatic successes. Powers don't need mortals to work, that's silly.<br /> <br /> If Thor throws a lightning bolt at Jormungandr, there doesn't need to be a mortal witness.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think I've seen the word &quot;RAW&quot; enough times here to know that no one really plays by the book rules... so.. if 1 to 5 dice ain't enough, make sure the penalties would be enough.<br /> <br /> No mortal witness, true but still fatebounds... maybe somehow we should link that to mortals... Gods would be untouchable otherwise since they would be no good reason to create any significant damages in the World unless they wanna fatebind themselves to millions of mortals.<br /> <br /> Well, my point is, if major penalties could be applied to powerful powers, players would play Gods in a more responsible way because playing Gods is not playing superheroes. Penalties make the game more interesting such as in Mage. The backfire should not restrict players to act but to act wiser.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T04:27:25-07:00","id":232664,"title":"","content":"This vague relationship between mortal man and the gods/titans is one of the things that needed to be better thought about in this game series. I totally agree with Telgar and Ajax; god created man so god could not possibly NEED man for anything, yet for god to <i>bother</i> creating man there has to be some kind of side-benefit that makes it worth the trouble of creating an intelligent species that can screw up the environment around it. I created a mechanic on my last home game that granted a bonus to PCs who had some kind of active cult dedicated to their worship, since otherwise mankind as a whole was largely an obstacle/annoyance. But it should be noted that this mechanic isn't absolutely necessary and shouldn't be. Having a bonus is great but the gods should be able to stand on their own power.<br /> <br /> Incidentally the supplement &quot;We are but Mere Mortals&quot; from biblioteque interdite further muddies the issue further by suggesting that mankind is a spontaneous outbreak from the early days when the titans ruled over nature and the gods did not exist. It describes the initial worship of vague elemental powers (i.e. titans) who ultimately did not care whatsoever as long as man knew his place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T09:33:38-07:00","id":232906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wickedgrail</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/218017-unveiled?p=232471#post232471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Well, my point is, if major penalties could be applied to powerful powers, players would play Gods in a more responsible way because playing Gods is not playing superheroes. Penalties make the game more interesting such as in Mage. The backfire should not restrict players to act but to act wiser.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gods don't have to be nice. In fact most aren't. They don't have to want to protect mortals. They can hate them and want to eat them. They can take the slightest insult or mistake and destroy cities, cause starvation, transform people into monsters, plants, animals or minerals. <br /> <br /> Most gods are the very definition of irresponsibility. Even the gods of prudence and good behavior act like downright assholes on occasion.<br /> <br /> If you want to play Hero by the modern definition of &quot;hero&quot;, that's cool. But that's not what the word &quot;hero&quot; meant originally. It just meant something like &quot;human with divine ancestors who is fated to do important stuff&quot;. And important stuff usually meant &quot;bad&quot; as well as good. If there was any good. Look at the legends of Hercules, Theseus and Jason for guys to whom that term was precisely defined.<br /> <br /> I'm in one game where the players are struggling as to whether to be good guys. It would sure make things easier to be self-interested jerks who could care less what happens to the mortals around us. Particularly those we don't know personally. We have one character who is a &quot;party conscience&quot;. Up until very recently, we made a point out of NOT listening to him. In a game I am running, the Scions pretty much think of mortals as pesky and pathetic that are occasionally useful. But not often. Sometimes the players are a little shocked at how callous their characters are. I've run other games where the characters were nicer people and acted more on behalf of the mortals around them and actually cared about humanity in the abstract. But that's a matter of my plotting and the characters chosen by the players and how they develop than it is by the mechanics or source material.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T14:02:12-07:00","id":233210,"title":"","content":"The issue with having mortals granting mechanical benefit to gods can be summed up in one word: Devas. When you have one pantheon with close to a billion active worshippers, orders of magnitude above most, if not all, of the others (more, even, than their likely historical peaks in terms of sheer number of worshippers, but I may be wrong there), you can create major dysfunction in terms of your game balance. Suddenly making a Deva character becomes the mechanically best choice.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying that having mortal worship have an effect on the gods is a bad thing. It isn't. But in order to both conform to the state of reality and also create a fun gaming experience, it has to be treated carefully. I'll be the first to admit that I don't know what the right choice about this is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Games are a way for us to explore what it means to be human, or inhuman, as the case may be. Let's all have a good time playing them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/400-guitarsniper","name":"guitarsniper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T17:00:51-07:00","id":235907,"title":"","content":"I don't see Scion that way. I'm not saying that every Hero should treasure mortals, no human can do that. But Heroes and Gods don't happen to hurt mortals that much. If you look at the Greek ones, they might have caused some pain to mortals. That's not really how the other pantheons work. Gods are powerful beings that can rule over mankind! In Scion, it's a little more subtle since you can't interact with mortals without creating Fatebindings. As Telgar said, Gods won't be affected by penalties described in the book and that's why I suggested that there should be new rules about that.<br /> Players should have fun despising mortals when they play Heroes already. But consequences are what create more interactions and stories for further games! There's no point if players could hurt mortals consequence-free, is there?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1837,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","user":"Wickedgrail","date":". 08-30-2014, 06:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T21:01:32-07:00","id":236152,"title":"","content":"Sure there is? They can be in drama with other Scions, Gods, supernatural beings.. there are many cultures where the mythology of the gods barely concerns itself with mortals at all. Try Sumeria, Egypt and Mesoamerica for some easy examples. There's some Scions in there, but not much in the way of Joe Mortal. And those Gods do some seriously nasty things to the <i>entire world</i> just for fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-30T15:21:42-07:00","id":245022,"title":"","content":"Then why those Gods won't go mess with the mortal World? Why would they hesitate to create any tsunamis or earthquakes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-30T17:37:26-07:00","id":245080,"title":"","content":"Because they know that they aren't alone in the world. It's one thing for Poseidon to go all earthshaker in the Mediterranean. But he knows he can't go to Norway to try that without getting his ass kicked up to his ears. The region and culture is against him. And I think you knew this. You just wanted someone to come out and say it. And I'm the guy for that! (am I wrong?) <img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-30T21:17:36-07:00","id":245170,"title":"","content":"That makes for some interesting jurisdictional conflict not unlike a spy movie. I can just see some group of demigods corraling a few foreign heroes and saying: &quot;Yeah we know there's a swarm of freaking drakes laying waste to the countryside, but it's OUR countryside, you stay your ass down in the Mediterranean and GTFO of our territory!&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T04:08:50-07:00","id":248741,"title":"","content":"Umm, Let's say Tlazolteotl (yeah, I know I spell it right haha) wanted to create an earthquake in Mexico. That's her territory right? But she won't because... well, bad example, I can't visualize her doing that... Well my point is, what about if one territory &quot;belongs&quot; to one pantheon. It would generate no conflict with other Gods... why would he still hesitate to do it for fun only, if that's how he has fun....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T07:09:21-07:00","id":248797,"title":"","content":"Hmm..the gods have an investment in the culture/region that they supposedly created, or that they arose from? That should make sense. &quot;Should...&quot;<br /> Ah...this leads to something that was brought up earlier in another thread.<br /> If the culture gets completely wiped out, what happens to that culture's gods? According to what some here contend those gods are still there because they aren't dependent on the culture that we would have known them from. Which means that we could have had that earthquake in Mexico centuries ago and completely obliterated the earlier culture. But what were the names of the gods then? We could have thousands of major league deities all about Mexico and we wouldn't have any idea what/who they are.<br /> While it make sense to assume that deities that created &quot;a world&quot; (i.e a culture) before there was one, to still exist long after it's gone...there seems to me a missing puzzle piece. And perhaps it's the &quot;why.&quot; Why create the culture to begin with? Empowerment perhaps? Whimsy doesn't answer the question, because that dismisses the order created.<br /> <br /> Lion Man was worshipped/revered 40,000 years ago in what would be Germany, or so we think. But what was the nature of this being?<br /> <br /> It's been said that a person lives after death as long as there is someone to remember him/her. Would this apply to gods? Would Lion Man have any influence on the much later worshipped world-creator Woden?<br /> <br /> ...sorry...train went off the track here...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T09:53:03-07:00","id":248940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wickedgrail</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/218017-unveiled?p=248741#post248741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Umm, Let's say Tlazolteotl (yeah, I know I spell it right haha) wanted to create an earthquake in Mexico. That's her territory right? But she won't because... well, bad example, I can't visualize her doing that... Well my point is, what about if one territory &quot;belongs&quot; to one pantheon. It would generate no conflict with other Gods... why would he still hesitate to do it for fun only, if that's how he has fun....</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Honestly, what makes you think that isn't exactly what happens? Tlazolteotl, or much more likely Tezcatlipoca, gets bored, decides their people need some fun, and cause disasters. Either the other local Gods stop them (because they have plans that don't involve earthquakes) or the earthquake happens. Earthquakes happen. Living in a time of myths and gods is dangerous, but so is living in the modern world. There have been a handful of quakes so devastating they've made world news, just in the last few years. The only difference in Scion would be that they're caused by Gods.<br /> <br /> There are tons of stories where Gods bring disaster to Earth through negligence, malice, boredom or as a side effect of something else they're doing. There are dozens, maybe hundreds, of Gods that just <i>don't care</i> if they cause harm to humanity. Let alone the ones that <i>enjoy</i> causing harm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T10:19:59-07:00","id":248955,"title":"","content":"That would explain their erasure from human memory...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T16:47:20-07:00","id":249285,"title":"","content":"Shadowflame: That's what I'm trying to figure out. There's no real answer. It all depends on the GM I guess...<br /> Telgar: True... I guess when you're a God, no rule is powerful enough to hold you back... not even other Gods...<br /> <br /> <br /> Then Fate shouldn't be so important in Scion then. If the only backfires apply to Heroes to a certain level, there's no use of making Fate such a big deal.... I mean less dice? Really?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T17:25:18-07:00","id":249314,"title":"","content":"From a human perspective, there wouldn't be a difference between the gods and titans then. And if that's the case, then the gods that claim to need human sacrifices to help fight off the end of all that is... such a claim would then be a lie. Which wouldn't surprise me one bit. /","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T18:46:18-07:00","id":249362,"title":"","content":"The Gods are generally more relatable and more understandable. They work on something approaching a level humans can grasp, whereas Titans are purely elemental, and generally antagonistic, beings. They really <i>don't care</i> about humans, any more than humans care about ants. Gods at least care about humans as much as humans care about, say, fish.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T20:15:33-07:00","id":249416,"title":"","content":"Really?<br /> By your own words:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/218017-unveiled?p=248940#post248940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are tons of stories where Gods bring disaster to Earth through negligence, malice, boredom or as a side effect of something else they're doing. There are dozens, maybe hundreds, of Gods that just <i>don't care</i> if they cause harm to humanity. Let alone the ones that <i>enjoy</i> causing harm.</div> </div> </div> </div>And if we want to inject something close to genuine history, I could certainly agree with this.<br /> <br /> But it still makes them no different than titans in the game. And we can finally state with certainty that human sacrifices are the big lie that humanity has been deluded into believing. Because humanity doesn't make a difference. How can it? The gods were o-so-powerful before humanity came into being, and they're supposed to still be o-so-powerful after they've destroyed the culture that believed in them?<br /> <br /> So, how to fix this little problem?<br /> <br /> By putting humanity on the table and realizing how potent a playing piece it can be when combined with the gods.<br /> Enter Scion.<br /> Of course, this wrecks the previous assertion that the gods remain as powerful without humanity's involvement.<br /> If two equal deities meet on an opposing field, but one has five scions (each of which is a one man army), I'd say that the one flying solo isn't going to be pleased. Especially given how active scions tend to be, creating more of a metaphysical support across the worlds for their parental deity.<br /> Of course this also adds the fact that the gods will have to play nice. They may be &quot;indifferent, negligent, malicious,&quot; but the scions won't be.<br /> <br /> Humanity; the wild card that the gods realized they needed almost too late.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T20:37:03-07:00","id":249430,"title":"","content":"Shadowflame, I don't even understand what you're arguing anymore. Of course Scions matter, that's the point of the game. The Titans aren't the enemies of the Gods because the Titans will wipe out Earth and humanity. They're the enemies of the Gods because <i>they want to wipe out the Gods</i>. Yes, both are dangerous to humanity. From a human perspective, both are equally dangerous. There's only so many levels of &quot;dead&quot; you can get, after all.<br /> <br /> What's your point? What's this mess about human sacrifices?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":235,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","user":"Telgar","date":". 09-04-2014, 11:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T20:51:36-07:00","id":249443,"title":"","content":"Your the one not making sense. You said that the gods remain powerful regardless of humanity. Do I need to repost your own words?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T21:18:50-07:00","id":249452,"title":"","content":"Are you talking about mythologically, or in terms of Scion? Because mythologically, the only Gods I've ever heard of who <i>need</i> humans are the Aztecs, who need blood to do their work because blood is the life energy of the universe. However in Scion terms, while blood certainly helps the Teotl out, it isn't <i>essential</i> for them.<br /> <br /> In Scion terms, Gods have <i>no need</i> for humans. Human belief does not create or empower them, or really threaten them in any significant way. <br /> <br /> Scions are powerful because of their divinity, not their humanity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-05T06:41:50-07:00","id":249734,"title":"","content":"Wickedgrail asked why a deity wouldn't go all destructor in his/her native region.<br /> I posited the idea that said deity would have an investment not to. (after reading my following post I should amend that to a deity having such an investment is in relative recent memory, since the gods of ages earlier that may have went out in a blaze of glory are long forgotten)<br /> I then continued my thought on regional cultures getting wiped out, with their respective gods...becoming forgotten. Adding to the earlier premise that the gods are always as powerful as they are regardless of humanity...hm..that does seem wrong.<br /> <br /> If the gods had beaten the titans before humans had been created...and don't need humans, but for some strange fucked up reason now need human sacrifices to beat the titans...then how did they beat them long before humanity's arrival?<br /> What does Moloch gain by burning babies alive after he allegedly helped in the titan beat down in that earlier time when humans didn't even exist?<br /> As it stands now, your posts read that there isn't any benefit humanity gains from the God vs Titan deal. It's like &quot;alien versus alien&quot; and the best that humans could hope for is indifference. In other words there isn't a difference between God and Titan. A scion would do just as well with a titan as s/he would with a god.<br /> <br /> Don't reject the Scion's humanity. To me, a scion represents added power to a divine parent, and a bridge between human and divine. (Or better to say an investment in humanity) If a divinity forgets this, and treats humanity in a way that offends the scion, it should be up to the scion to remind the parent to respect that connection.<br /> <br /> I hope that Scion2.0 explores the idea of disaffected scions that refuse the pantheon that their divine parent may have come from in search of one more to their liking...Or &quot;orphans&quot; snatched up by the wrong pantheon...but ideas that put humanity back where it should be; <i>in play</i>. Because scions aren't just divine, their human as well. And if the gods have an investment in humanity that represent &quot;poker chips&quot; to play with, the scions have an investment in humanity because it's a part of their lives.<br /> /","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","user":"Shadowflame","date":". 09-05-2014, 09:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-05T07:09:19-07:00","id":249761,"title":"","content":"Some Gods are quite friendly towards humanity. Some are not. Generally, all Titans are bad news for humanity. But just because Gods <i>can</i> be good for humanity (as some humans are a great help to animals) does not mean that <i>all</i> Gods are good or that there is anything forcing Gods to act nicely towards humans. It's their own personal choice.<br /> <br /> I <i>still</i> have no idea what you mean about human sacrifices. They like being honored, but aside from the Aztecs, they don't get anything from it except an ego boost. Moloch doesn't get anything from human sacrifice except the knowledge that humans fear and respect him so much they'll offer the sacrifice to keep him happy. He doesn't need it. He just likes it. <br /> <br /> And once again, Gods do not ever &quot;fade away&quot; even if their human society does. The Minoan Gods are still as vital and powerful now as they were thousands of years ago, same for the Scythian Gods and the Gaulish Gods. Obviously as <i>players</i> of the game, we have trouble incorporating them into the setting since we, as modern humans, know little or nothing about them. That doesn't mean that in the setting they don't still exist and have power.<br /> <br /> <b>In Scion, Gods are not created, sustained or fueled by belief or sacrifice</b>, with the exception of the Aztecs, who can gain <i>additional</i> Legend from blood rituals performed by their followers using a single PSP Boon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-05T09:08:08-07:00","id":249849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In Scion, Gods are not created, sustained or fueled by belief or sacrifice, with the exception of the Aztecs, who can gain additional Legend from blood rituals performed by their followers using a single PSP Boon. </div> </div> </div>Sacrifice is being adopted a bit more wholesale as an all-pantheon mechanic. <br /> <br /> Gods aren't created by worship or ideals, no, but there are reasons they want cults and followers, as we'll talk about in Origins and Hero.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-05T14:49:37-07:00","id":250146,"title":"","content":"Does that not give the Pantheons with active mortal religions a significant power advantage over everyone else? Can't say that makes for an appealing feature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-05T15:33:17-07:00","id":250182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/218017-unveiled?p=250146#post250146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does that not give the Pantheons with active mortal religions a significant power advantage over everyone else? Can't say that makes for an appealing feature.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's true, and it'll be interesting to see how it's handled, but having a mechanical incentive for players to create cults could make for some interesting play. Again, I think we'll have to see how it's handled in the mechanics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Games are a way for us to explore what it means to be human, or inhuman, as the case may be. Let's all have a good time playing them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/400-guitarsniper","name":"guitarsniper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-05T20:47:19-07:00","id":250405,"title":"","content":"An idea floating around for Scion 2.0 was the importance of Cults and Temples devoted to you granting you the use of the low-capital avatar ability and demonstrating powers within the areas of their influence, but disallow godly might elsewhere.<br /> <br /> It probably won't go anywhere, but I know the three of us are discussing the potential of mortals to do /something/' for the gods. So many mythologies have humanity useful even if it's just for labor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-05T21:05:17-07:00","id":250448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I still have no idea what you mean about human sacrifices. They like being honored, but aside from the Aztecs, they don't get anything from it except an ego boost. Moloch doesn't get anything from human sacrifice except the knowledge that humans fear and respect him so much they'll offer the sacrifice to keep him happy. He doesn't need it. He just likes it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Point missed again. A deity that enjoys having people killed = Evil. Moloch and him getting off on babies being burned to death? He's not one of the good guys here. Game-wise, only a scion that is a sadistic monster would want to have any association with him. Were I to play his scion...I'd be looking at Nyx for a replacement patron. (Yes, a titan looks real good in comparison) <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And once again, Gods do not ever &quot;fade away&quot; even if their human society does.</div> </div> </div> </div> It doesn't matter. You can't name the deities now can you? No one can. Memories are gone and that's it....I was never fond of the idea of a being that claims to be so powerful but can never seem to learn to be better. And yet humans can do just that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-05T21:19:36-07:00","id":250463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/218017-unveiled?p=250448#post250448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Point missed again. A deity that enjoys having people killed = Evil. Moloch and him getting off on babies being burned to death? He's not one of the good guys here. Game-wise, only a scion that is a sadistic monster would want to have any association with him. Were I to play his scion...I'd be looking at Nyx for a replacement patron. (Yes, a titan looks real good in comparison)</div> </div> </div> </div>What point? What <i>is</i> your point? I have been missing your point the whole time, because I don't understand what you're trying to say. What are you even arguing?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/218017-unveiled?p=250448#post250448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It doesn't matter. You can't name the deities now can you? No one can. Memories are gone and that's it....I was never fond of the idea of a being that claims to be so powerful but can never seem to learn to be better. And yet humans can do just that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> ...Whaat?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-06T02:06:05-07:00","id":250600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/218017-unveiled?p=250146#post250146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does that not give the Pantheons with active mortal religions a significant power advantage over everyone else? Can't say that makes for an appealing feature.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, it should. The more you're famous the more you're powerful. It's always been like this, even for celebrities. The Hindu must be one of the most powerful pantheons because they are still worshipped. White Wolf might have seen it that way and that's why they created Alliance Pantheon... you become powerful when mortals know you and acknowledge your power. That's what I like to believe because if humans are useless, I'm not sure why I would play Scion in the first place. I don't know how to make mortals more important or powerful yet but I think pantheons should be more or less powerful because of mortals. That's actually how we know the many purviews of Odin, right? His deeds were told by mortals and that's how the Aesir people work anyway. Tales. <br /> <br /> Telgar, you don't seem to like adding mortals in your games... it's somehow bothering you and... well, I guess we just have different point of views and we might never agree ^^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-06T07:03:20-07:00","id":250729,"title":"","content":"I have no problems with mortals, as long as they don't control Gods. If being worshipped gives you power, <i>why would the Gods allow themselves to be abandoned</i>? They don't have to. The Devas, Shen, Orishas, Yazatas and Kami didn't allow themselves to be abandoned. Why would the others? If Scion takes place in a setting where belief is literal power, then the Gods of Europe and the Middle East would <i>not</i> have accepted monotheism converting their worshippers. The Gods of the New World would not have accepted colonialism destroying their societies.<br /> <br /> That aside, it turns Gods into divine politicians, scrambling for the most &quot;votes&quot;. It turns power into a popularity contest. It's a very uplifting, post-modernist idea that makes modern people feel great. Humans are special! We have the ultimate power, even over <b>Gods</b>! It's our belief that fuels them, so we can control them! We are the narrators of reality! We decide, our choices matter! That's an entirely alien mindset to almost any ancient culture I've ever come across. It's <i>startlingly</i> new, existing for less than a hundred years. It's entirely out of place in mythology.<br /> <br /> No one worshipped Nergal because they thought their worship made him stronger. They worshipped Nergal because <i>otherwise he would strike them with plagues.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-06T07:24:28-07:00","id":250742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/218017-unveiled?p=250463#post250463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What point? What <i>is</i> your point? I have been missing your point the whole time, because I don't understand what you're trying to say. What are you even arguing?</div> </div> </div> </div>You continually posted above that the gods can be cruel and malicious, and nasty to humanity.<br /> I posted &quot;Yeah, human sacrifice is a good example.<br /> You were like &quot;So what?&quot;<br /> I was like all &quot;All powerful deity before humans were invented, then they claim to need to kill them?&quot;<br /> You were like &quot;Some don't need to. Some just enjoy inflicting torture and death.&quot;<br /> I was like &quot;&quot;what's the sense in playing a scion to a deity that enjoys killing people?&quot;<br /> Now you go &quot;I don't understand what you're trying to say...&quot;<br /> I go...&quot;Moloch burning babies to death..mmm..evil bad..k&quot;<br /> You go &quot;I still don't know your point? Is this English?&quot;<br /> I go...&quot;Titans are supposed to be the bad guys, but they look o so pretty now...&quot;<br /> <br /> Answer this; What's the sense in playing a scion of Moloch? Just answer that. (I don't think you will)<br /> <br /> Since humans are irrelevant, or worse simply slaves or toys (t<u>here should be something wrong with that.</u> Jim Butcher's take that humanity is a nuke waiting to go off everywhere, might be a better direction to go. I'm still thinking that one through.) then there isn't a difference between God and Titan.<br /> Palladium books &quot;Rifts&quot; have their version of deities, and I think the direction he took was a bit more right. In that the gods can learn to be more advanced. Certainly to learn to be a bit more better than to believe it's necessary to rip a human's heart out every day. (You'd think after centuries that they'd find another way. Epic Intelligence = Epic Fail) Humans can progress, but gods can't? Humans are vastly more different than they were when they worshipped these deities ages ago. That difference should be clearly noted.<br /> <br /> And in deference to the thread...if a scion of Moloch were to proudly claim himself as just that, in full frontal with a burning sacrifice at hand, then it should be open season on him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","user":"Shadowflame","date":".  clarifying sentence...all late too.. 09-06-2014, 02:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-06T14:20:11-07:00","id":251050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/218017-unveiled?p=250742#post250742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Answer this; What's the sense in playing a scion of Moloch? Just answer that. (I don't think you will)</div> </div> </div> </div>because it's fun and makes for an entertaining story? A Scion who spites his divine parent because of some reason is always something that's fun to play. Especially if the parent tries to win the adoration or loyalty of the Scion in question.<br /> <br /> Also, Moloch, who enjoys killing humans kinda need humans to kill to enjoy it. The titans are blind to humanity in such a way that they are elemental chaos. The titan of fire wants fire to be all there is. If the Titans won, the world would become utterly uninhabitable for humanity. The gods would be brought down to extinction and a long time would pass until the next generation of &quot;gods&quot; would arise to imprison the titans again.<br /> <br /> Personally, I'd love if belief and humanity had some effect. It could be as simple as a connection to fate. If enough &quot;fate&quot; is rolled, maybe a branding is permanent. You try to save that girl, dozens of successes are rolled and BOOM suddenly you have a permanent brand that makes it really difficult to not try to save all girls in trouble. This, applying only on earth, would really make it sensible for deities to retreat after a while.<br /> <br /> I mean, if Tor hangs around Scandinavia long enough, he'll soon have a lot of fatebindings that forces him to do stuff. This is something his enemies can abuse, so Tor retreats to Asgard to prevent this from happening. This would make no-longer worshiped gods equal to newer gods. I mean, they got a lot of fate bindings that might've been permanent back in the days. They are free from the short-term bindings, but can't gain short time bindings for profit either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/593-gemstone","name":"Gemstone","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-06T16:51:37-07:00","id":251144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/218017-unveiled?p=250729#post250729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have no problems with mortals, as long as they don't control Gods. If being worshipped gives you power, <i>why would the Gods allow themselves to be abandoned</i>? They don't have to. The Devas, Shen, Orishas, Yazatas and Kami didn't allow themselves to be abandoned. Why would the others? If Scion takes place in a setting where belief is literal power, then the Gods of Europe and the Middle East would <i>not</i> have accepted monotheism converting their worshippers. The Gods of the New World would not have accepted colonialism destroying their societies.</div> </div> </div> </div>They didn't allow it but weren't powerful enough to keep themselves <i>alive</i>. When monotheism came to them, what might have swung them to the other side is that the one God loves them all and won't play with mortals. That might be one of the good reasons for mortals to stop worshipping the ancient Gods and the one God was powerful too soon for other pantheons to fight back...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/218017-unveiled?p=250729#post250729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That aside, it turns Gods into divine politicians, scrambling for the most &quot;votes&quot;. It turns power into a popularity contest. It's a very uplifting, post-modernist idea that makes modern people feel great.</div> </div> </div> </div>But mythology was created by humans... I mean not in Scion, but we, humans wrote all those stories. Without us, those Gods wouldn't even be mentioned at all. I don't think it's that modern... and yeah, Gods are divine politicians. Even Scions. Why would an Egyptian Scion does good deeds and uses the Egyptian first Boon? To be acknowledge, to gain power, to become famous enough, to be feared by his enemies, to be loved by his fans (let's not talk about worshippers yet) and to become ultimately one of the Gods.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/218017-unveiled?p=250729#post250729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Humans are special! We have the ultimate power, even over <b>Gods</b>! It's our belief that fuels them, so we can control them! We are the narrators of reality! We decide, our choices matter! That's an entirely alien mindset to almost any ancient culture I've ever come across. It's <i>startlingly</i> new, existing for less than a hundred years. It's entirely out of place in mythology.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't really how you are able to know how mythology was viewed before but as I already said, mythology only exists because we wrote them to help humans understand the world in a magical way, which is a very beautiful and creative way <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/218017-unveiled?p=250729#post250729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No one worshipped Nergal because they thought their worship made him stronger. They worshipped Nergal because <i>otherwise he would strike them with plagues.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Does Nergal strike humans with plagues? What I mean is that, if that's what they were really afraid of, did plagues really strike humans when they stopped worshipping him?<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm not trying to make mortals more important than they should be in Scion. I guess I just want them to be more than a toy to Gods.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-06T17:16:25-07:00","id":251156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wickedgrail</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/218017-unveiled?p=251144#post251144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not trying to make mortals more important than they should be in Scion. I guess I just want them to be more than a toy to Gods.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm kind of wondering if this is the sticking point. Because, to some pantheons, that's kind of exactly what they were. Even the ones that don't treat them like toys often seem to treat them like mildly retarded sheep that need guiding so they don't wander off a cliff or something.<br /> <br /> In the scheme of things, mortals really <i>aren't</i> that important to most gods except as amusement, ego-gratification and labouring.<br /> <br /> If mortals were at all important, especially in the scope of the Scion game, the gods would have dropped in on the mortal government, explained what was happening and worked out how to get the mortals onside. Instead the gods are just doing what they need to do, and if that rides roughshod over the mortal way of doing things then too bad. And there's plenty of precedent of it in legend. Of course the Greeks are awesome examples of how mortals are simply there for one's gratification but I'm certain that most pantheons have similar stories.<br /> <br /> It sucks, and it's kind of the tragedy of Scion wherein the Scions are drawn away from the mortal ties they have and love, but it serves to highlight that mortals really don't have much importance in the scheme of godly things except as fodder, gratification and/or dudes/damsels in distress.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2608-squee","name":"Squee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2608_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-06T21:06:09-07:00","id":251217,"title":"","content":"I've had numerous PCs that were fine with killing people that got in their way, or for ritual reasons. Sometimes the PC's cling to their human morality, sometimes they leave it behind and become much more involved in divine thoughts and ways. So, yeah, I've had PCs that demanded ritual human sacrifice from their followers. Not because it granted them a mechanical benefit (it did not, as none of them had Itztli at a high enough level), but because it was culturally appropriate for their Pantheon. Others <i>performed</i> ritual human sacrifice because it was expected of them as Scions from Pantheons where that's a fairly standard practice. Or because it enabled certain Boons, or both.<br /> <br /> Not everyone is playing Scion to play a fights-evil-saves-the-day superhero-hero.<br /> <br /> Squee's post is great. He's bang on, the story doesn't have to be about humanity at all. Humanity can just be the damsel in distress, or the girlfriend in the refrigerator (check out Feminist Frequency). It can be the ball-n-chain that some Scions want to shed. The real story is about the Scions, who <i>aren't human</i>.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Wicked, I can't tell if you're talking about Scion or reality. In real history, the mythologies of Scion were all religions, believed and followed every bit as faithfully and fervently as any religion is today. So, yes, people <i>truly believed</i> that if they did not worship Nergal, he would smite them. If they angered Zeus, he would smite them. They believed that if they broke religious laws, they would suffer. If they did not make sacrifices, they would suffer. People continue to believe that today, all over the world, as monotheists and polytheists and everything in between. So, while yes, humans wrote all myths and developed all religions, that has never stopped the followers of any religion from believing <i>with absolute conviction</i> that their religion was handed down by the God or Gods who actually, in truth, in reality, created the whole world and everything in it.<br /> <br /> Gods &gt; Humans. That's just kinda how religion works. I honestly do not know of any organized religion that works differently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-06T23:35:23-07:00","id":251283,"title":"","content":"Well, going by the OP, if an event become too believable to be just ignored away, then IMHO, the pantheon that instigated the event may be worshiped more by people who are less skeptical than others. Also, the Abrahamic religions may have a few words (and/or threats) about this and seek to destroy said pantheon, in the name of God. As a side note, Theology majors may also increase, in order to understand this new paradigm.<br /> <br /> As for whether or not Gods need Mortals, I must say that in Scion: God (First Edition), they stated that the entities that became Gods were once part of the Titans, but then they were changed by the mass consciousness of humanity. Those that were in the Sahara became the Pesdajet, in the Mediterranean, the Olympians, and in Scandinavia, they became the Aesir. It was then that the change in their idenities made them doubt the Titans and seek to take over for the sake of Humanity.<br /> <br /> For this edition, I won't know what OP plans until they reveal the info.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-07T06:36:44-07:00","id":251424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackalopeVegas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/218017-unveiled?p=251283#post251283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, going by the OP, if an event become too believable to be just ignored away, then IMHO, the pantheon that instigated the event may be worshiped more by people who are less skeptical than others. Also, the Abrahamic religions may have a few words (and/or threats) about this and seek to destroy said pantheon, in the name of God. As a side note, Theology majors may also increase, in order to understand this new paradigm.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it would depend on the event. Most pantheons don't want to be seen as mere devils. And the major religions will make them into that for various reasons. (And that would be easy to prove by simply pointing out the deities that enjoy human misery as well as those that still believe they &quot;require&quot; human sacrifices to keep the world running.) And major governments will refuse to be seen as lesser powers, even if that meant going to war with the pantheon in question. All of which would be backed by Abrahamic belief. (Hindu needs a special mention, but I lack the time) And since we're talking game here, Abrahamic beliefs versus the pantheon in question would probably be very ugly. I don't think anyone wants to go there.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-07T06:39:48-07:00","id":251425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Squee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/218017-unveiled?p=251156#post251156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It sucks, and it's kind of the tragedy of Scion wherein the Scions are drawn away from the mortal ties they have and love, but it serves to highlight that mortals really don't have much importance in the scheme of godly things except as fodder, gratification and/or dudes/damsels in distress.</div> </div> </div> </div>If that's how you play the game, where the scion forgets his/her humanity, then I think what sucks is the Storytelling.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-07T08:02:47-07:00","id":251475,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Personal attacks are not permitted. Darksider</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":11,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","user":"Darksider","date":". 09-07-2014, 03:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-07T09:02:04-07:00","id":251498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/218017-unveiled?p=251217#post251217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've had numerous PCs that were fine with killing people that got in their way, or for ritual reasons. Sometimes the PC's cling to their human morality, sometimes they leave it behind and become much more involved in divine thoughts and ways. So, yeah, I've had PCs that demanded ritual human sacrifice from their followers. Not because it granted them a mechanical benefit (it did not, as none of them had Itztli at a high enough level), but because it was culturally appropriate for their Pantheon. Others <i>performed</i> ritual human sacrifice because it was expected of them as Scions from Pantheons where that's a fairly standard practice. Or because it enabled certain Boons, or both.</div> </div> </div> </div>I totally agree. As GM, I allow it as well and will sometimes make my players choose between humanity and following divine orders. So, I have no problem in making stories about killing mortals! Absolutely not!<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/218017-unveiled?p=251217#post251217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not everyone is playing Scion to play a fights-evil-saves-the-day superhero-hero.<br /> <br /> Squee's post is great. He's bang on, the story doesn't have to be about humanity at all. Humanity can just be the damsel in distress, or the girlfriend in the refrigerator (check out Feminist Frequency). It can be the ball-n-chain that some Scions want to shed. The real story is about the Scions, who <i>aren't human</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mostly agree. A Scion is half human and what makes it nice to play is to see how far a player will go to change or keep the personality of the Scion. But that's not why I'm talking about how mortals are important in Scion.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/218017-unveiled?p=251217#post251217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wicked, I can't tell if you're talking about Scion or reality. In real history, the mythologies of Scion were all religions, believed and followed every bit as faithfully and fervently as any religion is today. So, yes, people <i>truly believed</i> that if they did not worship Nergal, he would smite them. If they angered Zeus, he would smite them. They believed that if they broke religious laws, they would suffer. If they did not make sacrifices, they would suffer. People continue to believe that today, all over the world, as monotheists and polytheists and everything in between. So, while yes, humans wrote all myths and developed all religions, that has never stopped the followers of any religion from believing <i>with absolute conviction</i> that their religion was handed down by the God or Gods who actually, in truth, in reality, created the whole world and everything in it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I DO agree. <br /> <br /> <br /> I'm not saying that Gods don't play with mortals. Of course they do and that's because there are interactions between the divine and the mortals that Gods are feared or loved but either way worshipped.<br /> <br /> Mmh... in the end, it sounds not so important to argue for mortals anymore haha. Yeah, let's just get them killed, it's okay! I can't find them any more power, if they had XD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}